    "https://careers.utah.edu/experiential-learning/": {
      "title": "U Career Success",
      "description": "Experiential Learning – U Career Success Skip to content U CAREER SUCCESS MENU Students Career Coaches Internships+ Events International Student Resources Career Courses Resources and Tools Employers Employers Home Post a Job or Internship Starting an Internship Program Next-Level Engagement Career Fair Recruiting Campus Partners Campus Partners Home Workshops Co-Sponsor an Event U Career Success Leadership More Career Impact Awards Contact Us Search Site Powered by the University of Utah Powered by Search Campus U Career Success Career Coaches Recruiters & Employers Campus Partners Events Home Experiential Learning Experiential Learning Internships and more Build Your Skills and Resume With Experiential Learning Experiential learning includes more than internships—it encompasses a wide range of activities that bridge the gap between theory and practice. Here are some ideas to get you started: Engage in classroom projects Participate in on-campus research Volunteer to support your interests Join student organizations and assume leadership roles Try your skills in a case competition Take classes that offer employer connections Speak or debate in a public setting Perform in a cultural production Sign up for Spring or Fall Break adventures Study abroad and expand your world These experiences contribute to your personal and professional growth as well as your skill set. It's about learning by doing, making mistakes, and evolving into a well-rounded individual. Hands-on experience enables you to stand out in the job market, giving you a distinct advantage when it's your time to enter the workforce. Internships Internships are an important part of experiential learning. These immersive experiences provide insights into your chosen field, allowing you to apply theoretical knowledge in real-world settings. The benefits extend beyond the immediate learnings—internships often serve as a gateway to future employment. They can also tip you off that a particular line of work is not the best fit for you, directing you to choose better matches going forward. U Career Success is dedicated to helping you find the right internships. From refining your resume to preparing for interviews, we're here to support you every step of the way. To find your perfect internship, log in to Handshake and make an appointment with your career coach today! Other Opportunities to Gain Experience Crimson Projects The Crimson Projects program partners companies with students for work on projects in product management, product marketing, data analytics, data science, research, software development, and finance. Learn More The Hinckley Institute The Hinckley Institute specializes in connecting students of all majors to accredited internships in Utah, Washington, D.C., and in countries around the world. Learn More Community Champions First- and second-years intern for local small businesses and nonprofits. All majors welcome. Learn More Goff Strategic Leadership Institute Goff programs help students from all backgrounds learn how to confidently lead in the spaces they care about, though for-credit projects, internships, and more. Learn More Ivory Experiences Meet prominent business leaders and policymakers at a series of breakfast and lunch meetings and spend a day on Capitol Hill for a behind-the-scenes introduction to Utah government. All majors welcome. First- and second-year students are eligible to participate. Learn More Nantes University Exchange This exchange offers students from the University of Utah a unique opportunity to study at Nantes University, located in the Loire region of France. Learn More Step Up Internship Fund The Step Up Fund supports undergraduate students from any major who have been offered unpaid internships. Step Up interns may receive $13/hour for up to 19 hours/week for 11 weeks. Learn More Meet With Your Career Coach Ready for more personalized guidance? Schedule a meeting with your career coach today! Schedule An Appointment Students Log in to Handshake Events Employers Employers Home Post a Job or Internship Next-Level Engagement Career Fairs & Expos Recruiting Policies U Career Success 1731 E Campus Center Dr, STE 1300 SALT LAKE CITY, UT 84112 801-587-8687 Top Resources International Student Resources Other Campus Partners Contact Us © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF UTAH Nondiscrimination & Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy About the U Media Contacts"
    },
