    "https://careers.utah.edu/career-impact-awards/": {
      "title": "U Career Success",
      "description": "Career Impact Awards – U Career Success Skip to content U CAREER SUCCESS MENU Students Career Coaches Internships+ Events International Student Resources Career Courses Resources and Tools Employers Employers Home Post a Job or Internship Starting an Internship Program Next-Level Engagement Career Fair Recruiting Campus Partners Campus Partners Home Workshops Co-Sponsor an Event U Career Success Leadership More Career Impact Awards Contact Us Search Site Powered by the University of Utah Powered by Search Campus U Career Success Career Coaches Recruiters & Employers Campus Partners Events Home Career Impact Awards Career Impact Awards We Want Your Input Creating student success is a campus and community-wide initiative that incorporates motivated students, dedicated faculty, exceptional employers, and engaging alumni who go above and beyond. In an effort to recognize these individuals, U Career Success created the Career Impact Awards.  We need your help to find and recognize these outstanding individuals. Please review the awards and criteria below to nominate. Submit Nomination Internships of the Year Did you have a great internship/research experience this past year? U Career Success is seeking to recognize U students and their life-changing internship experiences. Ten winning internship submissions will be selected by a panel of judges to be recognized as Internships of the Year! The winners will be invited to attend our awards ceremony in April along with their internship supervisor or mentor. Submission To submit your internship/research experience for consideration, write a 300-word essay describing why your experience was exceptional. Successful submissions will focus on at least one of the following topics: Projects: What did you work on during your internship and how was it impactful on your student experience? Learning Opportunity: What did you learn from your internship experience that complimented your classroom work or that you couldn’t have learned anywhere else? Career Development Experience: What made your internship experience exceptional and how did it inform your future career plans? Eligibility Qualified students and experiences must: Be submitted by the student intern by the deadline. Be currently enrolled at the University of Utah. Have interned during the year of their submission. Students who complete an internship between January 2025 and January 2026 are still eligible for the award even if they graduate prior to receiving the award. An internship is a short-term, hands-on, supervised work experience with a professional organization that increases your knowledge of a professional career field. It differs from a part-time job or volunteer experience in that an internship is designed to increase your knowledge, allows you to develop additional skills, and provides quality supervision to guide and mentor you. Only one self-submission will be counted for Internship of the Year. Submit Nomination Career Mentor of the Year Please help us recognize our strong Career Mentors at the University of Utah! Nominate U faculty, staff, or alumni who have contributed to your career development or exploration. This can be someone who helped you figure out your career passions, who took the time to help you find resources, or who introduced you to a new possibility. We want to take the time to thank the people who are helping you figure out your career paths. How do I nominate a Mentor? Submission: In 1-2 paragraphs, please share how this faculty, staff member, or alumni helped you with your career development and/or exploration. Submit Nomination Students Log in to Handshake Events Employers Employers Home Post a Job or Internship Next-Level Engagement Career Fairs & Expos Recruiting Policies U Career Success 1731 E Campus Center Dr, STE 1300 SALT LAKE CITY, UT 84112 801-587-8687 Top Resources International Student Resources Other Campus Partners Contact Us © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF UTAH Nondiscrimination & Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy About the U Media Contacts"
    },
